 "notes": "Open smile, teeth visible. Source is a heavily upscaled, blurry JPEG: every lip edge is a soft ramp about 10 to 15 px wide at source resolution, so the boundary was put at the half-transition of each ramp (read from column profiles), and the realistic tolerance is about +-3 px (about +-1.5 px in probe space). Corrections to the BiSeNet draft were large: inner top edge moved down about 8 to 12 px (the draft counted the shaded lower half of the upper lip as mouth); lower lip bottom raised about 5 to 12 px at x 620 to 760 (the draft followed the chin shadow below the lip); outer top moved 1 to 4 px; both commissures re-placed; dark corner (buccal) areas treated as mouth opening. Draft IoU vs final 0.755, mean boundary shift 5.1 px. Ambiguous: inner top edge (shadowed lipstick vs mouth cavity), lower lip bottom around x 690 to 720, and the dark commissure regions.",
